    {
      "post_id": 48345,
      "author_username": "meizzwang",
      "author_user_id": 11,
      "timestamp_iso": "2022-06-08T21:22:01+00:00",
      "timestamp_epoch_ms": 1654723321000,
      "timestamp_raw": "Jun 8, 2022 16:22:01 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "The traps have mostly opened up now and many are pretty dang big!  Last year, they feasted heavily and every last trap was LOADED with insects, but this year, the insect population isn't as robust and not as many traps are well fed.  Will the traps next season be small?  We'll see!  Maybe they might catch insects later on, but if they don't, it wouldn't be much of a surprise if these shrink spring 2023. <br/><br/>Pics taken  mostly on 6/6/22:<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52132516048_d958cd6d00_o.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52132515773_23b3691315_o.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>The lids on some of these are almost hard to believe:<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52131473427_dec2e70a6c_o.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>An average giant one:<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52132735134_e1fd1713eb_o.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>So floppy!<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52132733859_dc2b27ed19_o.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>It's hard to capture size in the pic, but this thing is enormous!<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52132493241_af8e6d293e_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52132494721_82034c2387_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>",
      "body_text": "The traps have mostly opened up now and many are pretty dang big!  Last year, they feasted heavily and every last trap was LOADED with insects, but this year, the insect population isn't as robust and not as many traps are well fed.  Will the traps next season be small?  We'll see!  Maybe they might catch insects later on, but if they don't, it wouldn't be much of a surprise if these shrink spring 2023.\nPics taken  mostly on 6/6/22:\nThe lids on some of these are almost hard to believe:\nAn average giant one:\nSo floppy!\nIt's hard to capture size in the pic, but this thing is enormous!",
